Neural Networks\
- Nodes, Connection to nodes\
- hidden layers\
- parameters: weights, biases\
	- weights: pick up patterns\
	- bias: at which point is neuron meaningfully active (like a threshold) \
- activation functions: activation of nodes based on input\
	- take in weighted sum of activations from one layer + bias\
	- ReLU: Rectified Linear Unit: max(0,x) \
		- its like only when certain value is reached, do I consider the node / feature as relevant \
	- softplus\
- backpropagation\
	- loss function\
		- SSR: sum of squared residuals\
	- gradient descent\
		- derivative\
			- chain rule\
		- step size: slope + learning rate\
		- stochastic gradient descent\
			- random point per small subset/mini-batch (group of samples)\
	- initialize weights and biases\
		- bias = 0\
		- weights = random\
			- standard normal distribution \
\
- ArgMax and SoftMax\
	- find class with highest predicted probability \
	- ArgMax NOT an activation function -> not for backpropagation (no derivative)\\		- output: 0 or 1\
	- SoftMax used for training (backpropagation, has derivative)\
		- takes all values of output vector in consideration (could be negative even)\
		- preserve ranking, output between 0 to 1 (probability)\
		- normalization\
		- calculates probability of each value to be correct value???\
	- Temperature\
		- large T value -> give more weight to lower values\
