\
Transformer:\
- new: don\'92t just take each word in text input at a time but take all of the text at once (CONTEXT)\
- words encoded as tokens (vectors) -> represent meaning, position of that word (gain more context as they move through the NN)\
	- encoding / embedding: tale column from the embedding matrix\
- architecture:\
	- goal: refine embeddings so that more information / context is represented by embedding vector\
	- layers of Feedforward + Attention\
	- Feedforward / Multilayer Perceptron\
	- Attention mechanism:\
		- multi-headed attention consists of multiple heads of attention \
		- every head uses one key, query, value map / matrix -> result is proposed CHANGE to original embedding vector (like new direction)\
		- new / refined embedding = old embedding + (result entire multi-headed attention block)\
- embedding\
	- encode tokens as vector (size n), take column from embedding matrix\
	- embedding matrix (n x m)\
 		- columns: all tokens (number m)\
		- rows: features (number n)\
		- matrix consists of weights / parameters\
	- unembedding matrix (m x n)\
		- decode (feature) vector to vector of probabilities for tokens (size m)\
		- matrix consists of weights / parameters\
- self-attention head\
	- GOAL: each embedding vector later encodes context / meaning / features taken from other embeddings (earlier ones)\
	- attention pattern\
		- key\
			- query matrix (k x n) of parameters\
		- query\
			- query matrix (k x n) of parameters\
		- masking\
			- later tokens do not influence earlier ones\
		- softmax\
	- value\
		- value matrix (n x n) of parameters: in practice its 2 matrices (k x n, n x k )\
		- low rank transformation\
	- output matrix\
